  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Subsidy Asylum Access Localization subsidy framework DSH-MO 2024-2029 - &quot;Scaling Refugee Leadership Through the Resourcing Refugee Leadership&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to weave together direct funding, capacity building, and meaningful participation in order to address the systemic exclusion of RLOs and the communities they support and scale sustainable, community-led solutions aimed at legal services, livelihoods programming, education, access to essential infrastructure, and more.&#xA0;Through its flexible and sizable direct funding, Asylum Access will ensure that RLOs have the financing they need to both grow their programming to meet community needs and to participate in key decision making spaces. In order to support effective RLO programming and &#xA0;sustainability, equitable and localized capacity building models will be used to collaboratively address barriers to impact. Finally, in order to ensure participation in decision making is meaningful, the project will support grantees to prepare for successful advocacy and advocates to institutions for more meaningful inclusion.</narrative>
  </description>
